procfs module of LKD (Linux kernel on Darwin), private research code for the SailOver project.

No block of HyperLinux is copied into this module. HyperLinux src/proc_emulation.c, proc_names.c and device.c
were read as a reference for which paths programs open (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2025 Moritz Angermann
<moritz@zw3rk.com>, zw3rk pte. ltd.); the files here are written for LKD.

src/procfs/global.c (render_cpuinfo): the structure of /proc/cpuinfo and the list of CPUID bits that become flags
follow FEX-Emu Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/EmulatedFiles/EmulatedFiles.cpp GenerateCPUInfo
(commit 0df84d3, SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT, Copyright FEX-Emu contributors), rewritten in C with the Linux
spelling of three flag names. The FEX CLAUDE.md forbids submitting AI-generated code upstream: nothing here is
submitted to FEX.

Output formats restate those of the Linux kernel v6.12 (GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note for uapi): fs/proc/array.c,
fs/proc/task_mmu.c, fs/proc/base.c, fs/proc/meminfo.c, arch/x86/kernel/cpu/proc.c, drivers/base/topology.c. No kernel
source text is copied; only the printed formats and field orders, which are part of the user-space ABI.
